# Compiled / build output
target/
*.class
*.jar
!maven-wrapper.jar
*.war
*.log
*.log.*

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Maven wrapper (keep the jar, ignore temp)
!maven-wrapper.jar

# Temp files
*~
*.tmp
*.bak

# Development / scratch scripts
fix_*.py
.scratch/*.pid

# Local environment & secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets.*

# Node (if any frontend assets land here)
node_modules/

# Tool session state (security scanner / agent harness)
.agents/
.mimosa/
.workbuddy/
.zcode/
.pytest_cache/

# JVM crash logs (belt & suspenders; *.log is already covered)
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
.qa_tmp/

# Python bytecode from the alert-bridge unit tests run on the host
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Raw probe output from benchmark/observability/drill.ps1. The conclusions are written up in
# docs/research; the scrape dumps and log tails behind them stay on the machine that ran it.
benchmark/observability/evidence/
# Raw JMeter output. run-loadtest.ps1 leaves the .jtl and the generated HTML report on the
# machine that ran the test; only the small dated .json/.md pair under benchmark/jmeter/results/
# is committed. Without these two lines the first run would stage megabytes of CSV and HTML.
benchmark/jmeter/**/*.jtl
benchmark/jmeter/**/*-report/
# Raw transcripts from benchmark/migrations/rehearse-migrations.ps1. Same rule as the drill and
# the JMeter run: the step-by-step log stays on the machine, the summary under results/ is kept.
benchmark/migrations/evidence/
# A write-up about the project rather than of it, quoting internal assessments. It lives on the
# machine that runs the project and never in the public remote. Never add it back.
Nexus-Vibe-项目全量梳理.md
# Same reasoning, and this one was actually tracked once (added in 6a5312d, still reachable in
# history). Removed from the tree on 2026-09-14; the local copy now lives outside the repository.
docs/project-experience-refactored.md
# Backup sets (scripts/backup.ps1): belong on a second volume, and are never committable - db.sql.gz holds password hashes.
backups/

# One-off probe scripts written while migrating controller statuses. They read the tree and
# print a count; the conclusions they reached live in the tickets and docs/research instead.

# Throwaway build inputs and console logs from work done on this machine: host-built jars,
# images assembled when a container build could not reach its package mirror, and the drill's
# own stdout. Same rule as the evidence directory - the conclusions are written up in docs/,
# the bytes behind them stay here.
scratch/

# Audit deliverables dropped in by external review tools (gstack). They quote internal
# assessments, so they stay on the machine that produced them like the evidence directory does;
# the conclusions worth keeping were rewritten into docs/tickets and docs/research.
deliverables/
